  "title": "We’ve got a large number of you joining our community more recently… ...",
  "description": "We’ve got a large number of you joining our community more recently…  So here’s the gist of our latest project: Back when we were making “carbon nation,” it became clear to me (Peter Byck) that our soils offered a spectacular way to draw down carbon from the air - where it’s become a problem - and get it back into our soils, where it is sorely needed. (I learned this stuff from a bunch of really smart people)  The folks who were the best, fastest, and most profitable at making this carbon shift (from air to soil), were the cattle farmers and ranchers in the carbon cowboys documentaries. So now we’re bringing you “Roots So Deep (you can see the devil down there)” - a 4-part documentary series all about inventive farmers and maverick scientists building a path to solving climate change with hooves, heart and soil.  But one question we’re dying to know; even if the science shows that the adaptive way to graze is better for the land and the farmers’ pocket books, will the conventional farmers change, will they adopt a different method? We’ve got some exciting news coming for those interested in watching at home! Make sure you’re subscribed to our newsletter to be the first to know. #regenerativefarming #regenerativeagriculture #regenerativeag #regenerativefarm #regenerativeagriculturemovement #carbonnation #rootssodeep #farmers #farming #ampgrazing #carboncowboys #carbonnation #rootssodeep #soilhealth #regenag",
